        "original_id": "8af5bbe8-d19b-57ad-a7a4-d6a427107cc9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Q5 bus route, Q85 bus route\n- Places: Merrick Boulevard, Southeastern Queens, New York City, Jamaica Center, Rosedale, Green Acres Mall, Nassau County, South Valley Stream, Sunrise Highway, Valley Stream, Town of Hempstead\n- Concepts: public transit corridor, shopping mall\n\nFacts:\n- The Q5 and Q85 bus routes form a public transit corridor along Merrick Boulevard in Southeastern Queens, New York City, United States.\n- The Q5 and Q85 bus routes run from the Jamaica Center transit hub and business district to Rosedale, and continue to Green Acres Mall in Nassau County.\n- Green Acres Mall is an indoor shopping mall in South Valley Stream, New York, off Sunrise Highway in Nassau County near the border of New York City and the Incorporated Village of Valley Stream.\n- Green Acres Mall itself is in an unincorporated hamlet of the Town of Hempstead, while part of its parking lot and some stores on the north side are in the Village of Valley Stream.\n- Green Acres Mall has 1,800,000 square feet of gross leasable area.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
